WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.120
Speaker 1: We appear really genuinely to be
getting to the later phases of fighting the

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.050
coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:13.309
Even with the anti-war sentiment that is plaguing
much of the country, which we've talked about,

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:18.900
we are continuing to get more and more good
news about the next few months in terms of

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.490
the battle against the pandemic.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:26.660
Yesterday, we received really great news that
the Fizer vaccine has been approved for emergency

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.980
use for 12 to 15 year olds.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.540
This will allow middle school age students
to be fully vaccinated by the time school

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.470
starts in the fall.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.510
We're going to talk more about that approval
a little bit later on in the program.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.719
But the Fizer vaccine has been found to be
100 percent effective in a clinical trial

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:54.620
of more than 2000 adolescents in terms of
protection and creating a robust antibody

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.620
response.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.810
That's very, very good news.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:02.039
We also learned that even with the current
variance of concern, which include the British

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:07.189
variant, the South African, the Brazilian,
the California, the New York and the Indian

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:14.679
variants, we will likely not need a booster
for the Fizer vaccine in the next six to 12

00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:15.679
months.

00:01:15.679 --> 00:01:19.700
And since the Moderna and Fizer vaccines work
essentially identically, they're essentially

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.700
clones.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.289
We will probably not need a Moderna booster
either in the next six to 12 months.

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:26.890
Now, this is important to understand.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:32.520
The vaccines will be updated over the next
six to 12 months to to account for the new

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.429
variants at some point in the future.

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:41.630
A booster for already vaccinated people may
be needed, but it appears that already vaccinated

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.909
people will not need a tweaked booster in
the next six to 12 months.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:50.409
People vaccinated for the first time in the
next six to 12 months will start getting a

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:53.380
tweaked version that accounts for the variance.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.290
That's fantastic news.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:02.389
But then maybe as importantly as we've expected,
based on the vaccination data, cases and deaths

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:07.829
are continuing down and that should accelerate
as we approach 40 percent fully vaccinated

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:11.370
in the U.S. and then hopefully on to 50 percent.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:17.480
Recall that cases peaked at about 250, 5000
cases per day in January.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.599
I mean, just remember when we were saying
if we're not careful, we might one day see

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.200
100000 cases a day?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.340
Well, we got two and a half times that two
hundred fifty five thousand cases per day

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.790
in January.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.370
We're down about 85 percent from that level
to about 40000 cases per day.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.370
Still a lot.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.269
But that rate of decline is once again accelerating
by Memorial Day.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:42.489
It should be quite a bit below that.

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:46.040
And we've even had a couple of days in the
last week at the sort of twenty six, twenty

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.530
eight thousand cases per day level.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.569
That's a good sign in terms of deaths.

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:59.049
Recall that the pandemic high of more than
3400 deaths per day was in late January.

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:06.530
That number is now also down about 81 percent
from its peak, still 650 deaths per day.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.879
Still a tragedy, still a pandemic.

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:14.290
Still much work to be done, but going in the
right direction and on a slight delay from

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.959
the case decline, we're seeing another inflection
point where we are seeing faster decline in

00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:26.999
deaths down even to the 200, 300 level a couple
of days this week, some of the lowest numbers

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:29.019
in a very long time.

00:03:29.019 --> 00:03:34.260
Some states like Massachusetts recently reporting
a single day with zero deaths for the first

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.230
time and basically since the beginning of
the pandemic.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:43.730
Now, another bit of good news from the vaccination
front is that after nearly a month of declining

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.519
vaccinations, because, as we said, supply
was starting to exceed demand, most of those

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:53.549
who really wanted to be vaccinated have been
able to get vaccinated.

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:55.810
And we had to start work on the vaccine resistant.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:01.900
While the average daily vaccinations have
again started to go up, they bottomed out

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.579
at about one point nine million doses a day.

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:07.529
We're back up to two point two million doses
a day.

00:04:07.529 --> 00:04:12.700
And as I mentioned earlier, Pfizer has now
been approved for emergency use for 12 to

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.819
15 year olds.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:15.120
We'll talk about that in a moment.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.130
And hopefully that will increase the numbers
as well.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.970
More and more countries are opening for travel
in person.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:28.030
School in the fall is looking like close to
an absolute certainty, with many schools requiring

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.740
vaccination for students to come back to campus.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.790
But that's just the United States.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.660
This is a global fight.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:35.660
What is?

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:40.550
Happening globally, where vaccine access is
still a major problem, so the good news globally

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:48.590
is that after another new peak in cases, global
cases are now starting to trend down again

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:53.160
and are down about seven percent from that
new peak.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.630
Global deaths are also just starting to tick
down.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:03.640
And even in India, which was experiencing,
I mean, just incredible tragedy for the last

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:10.289
month, cases per day appear to have peaked
and have just slightly started to decline.

00:05:10.289 --> 00:05:15.830
It is going to be a very long road for India,
but you always prefer to see cases going down

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.830
rather than up.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.780
So that's the current panorama.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:23.949
A couple of other small things we're learning
that early caution about the protection of

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:27.080
vaccines was appropriate before we knew.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.610
Do they reduce spread?

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.850
How effective are they?

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:35.639
But as more and more health experts continue
to look at the data, they are increasingly

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:41.130
comfortable saying, listen, when you're vaccinated,
just about every activity is low risk.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:46.370
That doesn't mean stop following CDC guidelines
about masking indoors, about protecting others.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.610
All of this stuff.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:53.040
But personal risk is really, really low if
you were vaccinated.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.870
So nothing in this world is zero, no doubt,
but very good vaccine news.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.389
And we'll see where we are next week as far
as the numbers are concerned.

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:05.419
Let's now talk about the expansion of the
Fizer vaccine to 12 to 15 year olds.

